code-heldout/go-cli-feature/opencode-2/repo/main_test.go","patch":"Index: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/go-cli-feature/opencode-2/repo/main_test.go\n===================================================================\n--- /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/go-cli-feature/opencode-2/repo/main_test.go\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/go-cli-feature/opencode-2/repo/main_test.go\n@@ -153,9 +153,9 @@\n \t{\n \t\tname:       \"min length with several files\",\n \t\targs:       []string{\"-min-length\", \"3\", \"{tmp}/a.txt\", \"{tmp}/b.txt\"},\n \t\tfiles:      map[string]string{\"a.txt\": \"ab abc\", \"b.txt\": \"abcd ab\"},\n-\t\twantStdout: \"1\\tabcd\\n1\\tabc\\n\",\n+\t\twantStdout: \"1\\tabc\\n1\\tabcd\\n\",\n \t},\n }\n for _, tt := range tests {\n \tt.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"main_test.go","time":{"start":1794861916150,"end":1794861916179}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait, \"min length counts characters not bytes below threshold\" case: min-length 4 with \"été et é\" → \"été\" is 3 chars → filtered out → empty output. Good.\n\nAlso for the \"min length and json with a file\" case: file \"one two three\" with min-length 4 → \"one\"(3) filtered, \"two\"(3) filtered, \"three\"(5) kept → `[{\"word\":\"three\",\"count\":1}]`. Good.\n\n\"min length with several files\": a.txt \"ab abc\", b.txt \"abcd ab\" → words: ab, abc, abcd, ab → with min-length 3: abc(1), abcd(1) → sorted alpha: abc, abcd → \"1\\tabc\\n1\\tabcd\\n\". Wait my expected is \"1\\tabcd\\n1\\tabc\\n\" — wrong! Alphabetical: \"abc\" < \"abcd\". So expected \"1\\tabc\\n1\\tabcd\\n\". Let me fix.\n\nAlso \"json format is a single line\" case: words a,b,c,d each count 1 → sorted alpha a,b,c,d → matches.\n\nLet me fix the several-files expectation.\n\nAlso I should double check the default text output case ordering: \"The cat sat. The cat ran!\" → words: the, cat, sat, the, cat, ran → counts: the=2, cat=2, sat=1, ran=1. Sorted: count desc, then alpha: cat(2), the(2), ran(1), sat(1) → \"2\\tcat\\n2\\tthe\\n1\\tran\\n1\\tsat\\n\". Matches.\n\nAlso the count package test for SetMinLength — add table-driven test in count_test.go.\n\nAlso note: `run` for the \"-format\" with file and stdin — when files are given, stdin is ignored. Fine.\n\nOne more: in the \"min length applies before top\" case, \"-top 2\" — with min-length 2 all words are 2 chars: aa, bb, cc, dd all count 1 → top 2 → aa, bb. Good.\n\nLet me fix the file case expectation and add count tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e61b5fbe001Nm0JV5GH63ssDV","sessionID":"ses_e19e5d7ecffePNEyqFpYUowKn6","messageID":"msg_1e61b4027001kuGFfAu3Hu8GRf"}}
