{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794861939996,"sessionID":"ses_e19e5d7ecffePNEyqFpYUowKn6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_2fa7139a678041e4b146d09d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/go-cli-feature/opencode-2/repo/README.md","newString":"```bash\ngo run . -top 5 notes.txt more.txt   # the five most frequent words over both files\ngo run . < notes.txt                 # read standard input; default -top 10\ngo run . -min-length 4 notes.txt     # ignore words shorter than four characters\ngo run . -format json notes.txt      # one line of JSON instead of the text output\ngo test ./...\n```\n\nA word is a run of letters, digits and apostrophes, compared in lower case. Output is one\n`count<TAB>word` line per word, most frequent first, ties in alphabetical order. Errors go to\nstandard error as `wordstat: <message>` with exit status 2 (bad flags) or 1 (unreadable file).\n\n`-min-length N` ignores words shorter than N characters (characters, not bytes, so `été` has\nlength 3) and defaults to 1, which counts every word. `-top` applies after the filter.\n`-format json` prints a single line with a JSON array of `{\"word\": \"...\", \"count\": N}` objects in\nthe same order as the text output (`[]` when there are no words); `-format text` is the default.\n","oldString":"```bash\ngo run . -top 5 notes.txt more.txt   # the five most frequent words over both files\ngo run . < notes.txt                 # read standard input; default -top 10\ngo test ./...\n```\n\nA word is a run of letters, digits and apostrophes, compared in lower case. Output is one\n`count<TAB>word` line per word, most frequent first, ties in alphabetical order. Errors go to\nstandard error as `wordstat: <message>` with exit status 2 (bad flags) or 1 (unreadable file).\n"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostic