{"type":"text","timestamp":1794861948770,"sessionID":"ses_e19e5d7ecffePNEyqFpYUowKn6","part":{"id":"prt_1e61bcb57001Y3bckuYKKMj7PO","messageID":"msg_1e61bc75a0017AxkXb89qz77O5","sessionID":"ses_e19e5d7ecffePNEyqFpYUowKn6","type":"text","text":"Done. Both flags are implemented and tested.\n\n**`internal/count/count.go`**\n- `Counter.SetMinLength(n)` (count.go:51) — words shorter than `n` are skipped while counting, measured in runes via `utf8.RuneCountInString` (so `été` is 3).\n- `Entry` gained `json:\"word\"` / `json:\"count\"` tags so the CLI can marshal it directly.\n\n**`main.go`**\n- `-min-length N` (default 1) and `-format text|json` (default `text`), validated right after flag parsing: `wordstat: -min-length must be 1 or more` and `wordstat: -format must be text or json`, both on stderr with exit 2.\n- `-top` still applies after the length filter (filtering happens during counting, ranking after).\n- `json` format prints one line: `[{\"word\":\"the\",\"count\":2},...]` in the same order as the text output, `[]` when empty. HTML escaping is off so words keep their characters. Text output, other error messages and exit codes are unchanged.\n\n**Tests** — new table-driven `main_test.go` (24 cases: filtering, rune counting, filter-before-top, both formats, both error paths, file/stdin/multi-file inputs) plus `TestMinLength` in `internal/count/count_test.go`. `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `gofmt -l` are all clean.","time":{"start":1794861943639,"end":1794861948766}}}
